course: dictionary
lesson: 15327
title: Snipping: quick, small cuts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Snipping means cutting with quick, short cuts, usually with scissors. Look at the words around it for clues. «Mia was snipping paper stars for the class display.» Paper and stars tell you that Mia is cutting paper, not painting or folding it.
explain: Snipping can also mean cutting small bits off something, like hair, paper or a plant. «Grandma was snipping dead roses off the bush.» The word roses tells you what gets cut off, and dead tells you why.
explain: On a computer, the snipping tool lets you cut out a part of the screen. Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if "cutting" still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Snipping means cutting something with quick, short cuts, usually with scissors.
fact: «Snipping» can also mean cutting small bits off something, such as hair, paper or a plant.
fact: «Snippings» is a noun: it means the small pieces cut off.
fact: Informally, snipping can mean cutting a small part out of a text, picture or video.
fact: A good check is to swap in "cutting" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Mia was snipping paper stars for the class display.» What is Mia doing to the paper? | Tearing it into one big piece | Folding it into a boat | Painting it bright colours | *Cutting it with quick cuts
exercise: «Grandma was snipping dead roses off the bush.» Which word tells you what Grandma was cutting off? | *roses | garden | Grandma | bush
exercise: Tom says snipping means chopping down a tree. What does snipping really mean? | *Cutting small bits off with quick, short cuts | Chopping a big tree down | Sweeping the floor clean | Carefully sewing cloth together
test: «Snip, snip, went the scissors as Tom cut the string.» What does the sound show? | Someone singing | A slow, loose cut | A loud crash | *Quick, careful, short cuts
test: Sam used the snipping tool to copy a picture from the game. What does snipping mean here? | Turning the computer off | *Cutting out a part of the screen | Breaking the screen | Printing the whole screen
exam: «After the haircut, the floor was covered in snippings.» What are the snippings? | A pair of scissors | *The small pieces cut off | The floor itself | Long, tidy hair still on the head
